body:
Vesting contracts release tokens to a beneficiary gradually over time instead of all at once -- commonly used for team allocations, investor tokens, or employee compensation, to align long-term incentives.

EXAMPLE (linear vesting):
uint256 public start;
uint256 public duration;
uint256 public totalAmount;
uint256 public released;

function releasable() public view returns (uint256) {
    if (block.timestamp < start) return 0;
    uint256 elapsed = block.timestamp - start;
    if (elapsed >= duration) return totalAmount - released;
    return (totalAmount * elapsed) / duration - released;
}

function release() external {
    uint256 amount = releasable();
    released += amount;
    token.transfer(beneficiary, amount);
}

WHY IT MATTERS: Vesting schedules are a trust signal in tokenomics -- a team that can dump all their tokens on day one gives holders no confidence in long-term commitment. OpenZeppelin's VestingWallet is the standard audited implementation.

FURTHER READING:
- OpenZeppelin VestingWallet docs: https://docs.openzeppelin.com/contracts/api/finance#VestingWallet
- Solidity docs, Common Patterns: https://docs.soliditylang.org/en/latest/common-patterns.html

